 short' claim rests on an unstated conversion. (3) With that implied constant, matching 2m_e needs net = 1.228289886, hence phi = 0.0538675 and s = 0.108282. The block quotes phi = 0.0487 and s = 0.0978, both low by a factor 1.106-1.107. (4) Worse, the quoted values give net_linear = 1.205278412 and net_circular = 1.205164840, both BELOW the bare 1.209060299. Under any increasing net-to-energy map the coloured configurations therefore have LESS energy than the bare pair and cannot close a shortfall - they widen it (E = 1.0029 and 1.0028 MeV against the bare 1.006). (5) Separately, phi and s are FITTED to 2m_e by construction ('Setting E_pair = 2m_e fixes phi = 0.0487'), so 'both models close the gap' would be a tautology even with correct values, not a prediction. (6) The algebra itself is CORRECT and was verified term by term: the five normal-form coefficients, net = (1 + phi_0 + phi_1)(1 + psi_0 + psi_1) + (phi_0 psi_0 + phi_1 psi_1)h, and both polarization specialisations all check out.","history":3},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:e00","notes":"STANDING-TRAP FINDING, report only: 'The gamma-gamma product directly opens the e^- (trefoil) channel' inherits the mis-identification in def:breit-wheeler-pair-production - see that block's notes. sigma_0 sigma_1 is also called L_+ ('provides Hopf-link dressing'), but its closure has ONE component (computed), so it is not a Hopf link; L_pm in section 7a denote crossing states rather than links, so this is at best an overloaded symbol.","history":3},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"warn","stale":false,"freshness":"fresh","at":"2026-11-24","reviewer":"script","by":"pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","h